# openbrain-cron — single source of truth for scheduled jobs.
#
# Bind-mounted from the host (../docker/cron/crontab). Edit freely, then
# `docker compose restart openbrain-cron` to reload.
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TIMING IS IN UTC
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The container runs in UTC (no TZ env var set). To convert your local
# time to UTC for a crontab entry:
#
#   Local TZ        Offset  Local → UTC
#   EDT (summer)    UTC-4   add 4h   (01:00 EDT → 05:00 UTC)
#   EST (winter)    UTC-5   add 5h   (01:00 EST → 06:00 UTC)
#   PDT (summer)    UTC-7   add 7h
#   PST (winter)    UTC-8   add 8h
#
# DST gotcha: a fixed UTC time drifts by 1h relative to local time twice
# a year. The default below is set for EDT (summer). At the November DST
# transition, bump the hour by +1 to keep "01:00 local" intent.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Trigger model is **event-chained**, not multi-cron. Cron only fires the
# start of the chain (pull). On success:
#   pull   → POSTs http://openbrain-gmail-prune:8080/run  (NEXT_TRIGGER_URL on pull)
#   prune  → POSTs http://openbrain-digest:8080/run        (NEXT_TRIGGER_URL on prune)
#   prune  → also triggers wiki recompile (separate, inside the script)
#   digest → end of chain
#
# This guarantees digest sees the latest pull's output. If any step
# fails, the chain stops — absence of the morning digest signals an
# upstream problem.
#
# To schedule a new top-of-chain job: add a line below pointing at the
# service's /run endpoint. To insert a step into an existing chain:
# adjust the relevant NEXT_TRIGGER_URL env in docker-compose.scheduled.yml.

# Daily ingest cascade. Set for 01:00 EDT (= 05:00 UTC). Digest arrives
# ~15–30 min later depending on how many new emails the pull processes.
#
#   window=90d: re-check the trailing 90 days every run. Dedup via the
#   pull's sync-log (gmail_id-keyed) and the brain's content fingerprint
#   short-circuits already-ingested emails, so the heavy work (LLM
#   metadata + embeddings) only happens for truly new emails. Daily
#   incremental cost is low; the wide window catches retroactive
#   labeling (e.g. tagging an old email brain/* yesterday).
#   limit=500: ceiling on a single pull, not the typical case.
#
# To change the firing time: edit the first two fields (minute hour).
# Examples:
#   0 5 * * *   → 05:00 UTC = 01:00 EDT / 00:00 EST
#   30 11 * * * → 11:30 UTC = 07:30 EDT / 06:30 EST
#   0 12 * * 1  → noon UTC every Monday only
0 5 * * *   curl -fsS -X POST -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"labelsPrefix":"brain/","window":"90d","limit":500}' http://openbrain-gmail-pull:8080/run

# Grounding backfiller (S2) — bounded off-peak GLOBAL sweep, 07:00 UTC (= 03:00
# EDT), after the daily chain has settled the day's new claims. Drains the
# `ungrounded_claims` view: per claim → entity → Wikipedia `corroborates` source
# → confidence recomputes → claim leaves the view. Brain-health for EVERY inlet
# (not just the podcast). Bounded (limit=50/run); un-groundable claims stamp
# backfill_skip so they're never re-attempted (no retry storm). Stand-alone, not
# chained — independent of the email pipeline.
0 7 * * *   curl -fsS -X POST 'http://openbrain-grounding-backfiller:8000/backfill?limit=50' || true

# Source re-fetch (S2) — heal thin/failed web sources whose original ingestion
# truncated them to ~150-char stubs. 07:30 UTC, after the backfiller sweep.
# Tor-first/direct-fallback; recovered → content updated (chunk-worker re-embeds);
# 3 attempts then marked refetch_failed (no retry storm). Bounded (limit=120/run).
30 7 * * *  curl -fsS -X POST 'http://openbrain-grounding-backfiller:8000/refetch?limit=120' || true

# Idea Refinery drain (IR.1) — researches owed ideas gently at 03:00 UTC (= 23:00
# EDT), WELL BEFORE the 05:00-UTC gmail/wiki chain, so the night's new claims land
# before the 1am-local wiki compile (the flywheel). Stand-alone, not chained.
# Bounded submit-on-complete + rollover; a persistently-failing idea gives up after
# 3 attempts (no retry storm). `|| true` so a fire while the (profile-gated) service
# is absent is a harmless no-op until IR.2 ships and it goes live.
0 3 * * *   curl -fsS -X POST 'http://openbrain-idea-refinery:8080/run' || true
